Refuse a GL that returns no version string instead of crashing on it.

The GPU process in a native child of its own crashed in its first half
second, every time: SIGSEGV in strlen, from FunctionsGL::initialize via
DisplayEGL::createRenderer. glGetString(GL_VERSION) had returned null --
no current context, or a driver that would not answer in that process --
and it went straight into a std::string.

On OHOS a null version is now read as version 0.0 of GLES, which
DisplayEGL refuses, so EGL initialisation fails and Chromium's own
fallback takes over instead of the process dying. The extensions string
gets the same guard. This does not make GL work in that process; it
makes a GL that does not work fail the way the rest of the stack
expects.

Generated for ANGLE 5382ed032a48ca6fefe8c3bca2c3c7c8edb8b63c (Chromium
154.0.8037.51).

diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/FunctionsGL.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/FunctionsGL.cpp
--- a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/FunctionsGL.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/FunctionsGL.cpp
@@ -21,7 +21,19 @@ static void GetGLVersion(PFNGLGETSTRINGPROC getStringFunction,
                          gl::Version *outVersion,
                          StandardGL *outStandard)
 {
-    const std::string version = reinterpret_cast<const char *>(getStringFunction(GL_VERSION));
+    const char *rawVersion = reinterpret_cast<const char *>(getStringFunction(GL_VERSION));
+#if defined(ANGLE_PLATFORM_OHOS)
+    // No current context, or a driver that will not answer: glGetString
+    // returns null, and constructing a string from it was a segfault in
+    // strlen. Version 0.0 makes the caller refuse the context instead.
+    if (rawVersion == nullptr)
+    {
+        *outStandard = STANDARD_GL_ES;
+        *outVersion  = gl::Version(0, 0);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
+    const std::string version = rawVersion;
     if (version.find("OpenGL ES") == std::string::npos)
     {
         // OpenGL spec states the GL_VERSION string will be in the following format:
@@ -83,6 +95,9 @@ void FunctionsGL::initialize(const egl::AttributeMap &displayAttributes)
     else
     {
         const char *exts = reinterpret_cast<const char *>(getString(GL_EXTENSIONS));
+#if defined(ANGLE_PLATFORM_OHOS)
+        if (exts != nullptr)
+#endif
         angle::SplitStringAlongWhitespace(std::string(exts), &extensions);
     }
 
